    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\square=7$, $\\triangle=6$.\n\nUse the last-three-digits test for 8 and the digit-sum test for 9.",
      "worked": "Since $72=8\\times9$, the number must be divisible by both 8 and 9.\n\nIts last three digits form a number from 250 to 259. The only multiple of 8 in this range is $256=8\\times32$, so $\\triangle=6$.\n\nThe digit sum is $\\square+7+2+5+6=\\square+20$. Since the first digit is from 1 to 9, this sum is from 21 to 29. The only multiple of 9 in that range is 27, so $\\square=7$.\n\nCheck: $77256=72\\times1073$.\n\nTherefore $\\square=7$ and $\\triangle=6$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
